    "warn · root › Stack[6] · Put <ContentCard>'s children back in the order ContentCardHeader, ContentCardBody, ContentCardFooter.",
    "warn · root · Dropped a child — <ContentCardHeader> only goes directly inside <ContentCard>, not <Stack>.",
    "info · root · Set align to "stretch" on the root (was "start") — the stack that holds the components always stretches.",
    "info · root · Set justify to "start" on the root — master layouts don't use static center alignment; the anchored group follows the focus instead.",
    "warn · root · Un-anchored an extra <Button> — a frame anchors at most one element group (kept the last).",
    "info · root · Made the root a column, keeping its children stacked in order — on level 1 the outermost container must be a column.",
    "warn · root · Set interactionState to "default" on <InteractivityButton> — a TV screen focuses one element, and <InteractivityButton> already has it.",
    "warn · root · Still breaks a layout rule — Level 1 (Home): focus is on root › Stack[0] <InteractivityButton> — Focus starts on the main menu — on the program button by default; when the Home rail sits on the left, on the left button that owns it (miscellaneous, schedule or login). A focus on an interactivity button would already be the second level.",
